      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lentor_MRT_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Designed by SAA Architects, Lentor’s columns mimic tree branches, letting natural light flood the underground concourse like a rainforest canopy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lentor_MRT_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Construction used a top‑down method to avoid damaging the major telecommunication cables that run beneath the station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lentor_MRT_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The station serves Lentor Estate, Teacher’s Estate, Anderson Primary School and the Saint Thomas Orthodox Syrian Cathedral.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lentor_MRT_station"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Lentor is a Civil Defence shelter, equipped with blast doors and air vents that can be sealed during a chemical attack.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lentor_MRT_station"
    },
    {
